Theorem RL-15: non-escaping dynamic-size allocation via function-local bump allocator

  Preconditions:
    - RL-15 governs dynamic-size stack promotion per Annex E §AIMS
      Stack Promotion: non-escaping dynamic-size values
      (Locality <= FunctionLocal) SHALL use a function-local bump allocator;
      bump objects retain RC headers if Uniqueness != Unique; the bump region
      is freed at function return.
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - DP-8 (is_local) gates locality. A dynamic-size value cannot use a fixed
      alloca slot, so a function-local bump region is the stack-equivalent.
    - Shipped: realize/decide.rs Locality consumption; repr.md sec-RH-3.
    - depends-on sec-05: DP-8 (is_local).

  Soundness property:
    Forall dynamic-size local value v (Locality <= FunctionLocal):

      (P1) Strategy decision: RL-15 selects a function-local bump allocator,
           for both Unique and MaybeShared locals.

      (P2) Lifetime soundness: a function-local bump region cannot outlive the
           function (the value is non-escaping), so freeing the bump region at
           function return releases every bump object exactly once — no object
           dangles and none leaks.

    RL-15 refines plain ARC by avoiding individual heap allocation + RC
    tracking for dynamic-size values that provably do not escape the frame.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine.

    Part (P1/P2) — dynamic-size local strategy:
      The verifier asserts that a local (BlockLocal / FunctionLocal)
      dynamic-size value (Unique / MaybeShared) selects BumpAlloc.
      Coverage gate: 4 cases (Block/Function x Unique/MaybeShared). Negative
      witness: an ESCAPING dynamic-size value must NOT use the function-local
      bump (it would dangle after the bump region is freed at return) -> heap.

    Engines dispatched:
